    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite (the single `AcceptanceTest` class) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` response flag: **true when more than 80 owners have already been created today, otherwise false**.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `bulkSignupWarning` (boolean, `readOnly`) property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Added a helper and wired it into both response paths:\n   - New `isBulkSignupWarning()` helper returns `countOwnersRegisteredOn(toBusinessDay(LocalDate.now())) > 80`. It reuses the existing `countOwnersRegisteredOn(...)` counting logic and the same business-day-resolved \"today\" that the per-day create-limit rule uses, keeping the accumulation path consistent (as the test's doc note describes).\n   - `addOwner` (POST) sets `ownerDto.setBulkSignupWarning(...)` on the created response.\n   - `getOwner` (GET) sets it too, since it's a request-scoped derived value not persisted on the entity \u2014 the acceptance test reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Design notes:**\n- The value is computed at response time (not stored), which is correct since it reflects the current global daily count, not a per-owner attribute.\n- `> 80` implements \"more than 80\" precisely (owner #81 triggers the warning).\n- Used `toBusinessDay(LocalDate.now())` so \"today\" matches the registration date the create path actually stores (today, 2026-09-05, is a Saturday and rolls to Monday 2026-09-07 \u2014 visible in the audit log during the test run).\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
